---
import StandardPageLayout from "../../layouts/StandardPageLayout.astro";
import Glossary from "../../components/Glossary.astro";
import PageToc from "../../components/PageToc.astro";
import "../../styles/standards-poster.css";
import "../../styles/extended.css";
import HistoryTimeline from "../../components/HistoryTimeline.astro";
import history from "../../data/history.json";
import metadata from "../../data/standards/aspe/aspe3475.json";
---

<StandardPageLayout
  code={metadata.code}
  standardType={metadata.framework}
  title={metadata.title}
  description={metadata.description}
  issued={metadata.issued}
  latestAmendment={metadata.latestAmendment}
  status={metadata.status}
  summary={metadata.summary}
  bannerNotice={metadata.bannerNotice}
>
  <Fragment slot="toc">
    <PageToc
      items={[
        { id: "s1", label: "Conceptual Framework Linkage" },
        { id: "s2", label: "Scope" },
        { id: "s3", label: "Held-for-Sale Classification Criteria" },
        { id: "s4", label: "Measurement Once Held for Sale" },
        { id: "s5", label: "No Further Depreciation While Held for Sale" },
        { id: "s6", label: "Discontinued Operations — Definition" },
        { id: "s7", label: "Presentation of Discontinued Operations" },
        { id: "s8", label: "Worked Example — Classifying an Asset as Held for Sale" },
        { id: "s9", label: "Worked Example — Presenting a Discontinued Operation" },
        { id: "s10", label: "Disclosure Requirements" },
        { id: "s11", label: "Critical Judgments &amp; Estimates" },
        { id: "s12", label: "Relationship to IFRS 5" },
        { id: "s13", label: "Statement Mapping" },
        { id: "s14", label: "Related Standards" },
        { id: "s15", label: "Glossary" }
      ]}
    />
  </Fragment>
  <div class="wrap">



<div class="section-header" id="s1"><span class="num">1</span><h2>Conceptual Framework Linkage</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Presenting held-for-sale assets and discontinued businesses distinctly from ongoing operations</div><div class="principle">ASPE Section 3475 governs the CLASSIFICATION and MEASUREMENT of LONG-lived assets HELD for SALE, and the PRESENTATION of DISCONTINUED operations SEPARATELY from CONTINUING operations WITHIN the INCOME Statement (see the COMPANION Section 1520 poster). THE Section is BROADLY converged with the GENERAL approach ALSO used INTERNATIONALLY under IFRS 5.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s2"><span class="num">2</span><h2>Scope</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Long-lived assets or components an enterprise intends to dispose of</div><div class="principle">This Section applies TO long-LIVED assets (OR groups OF assets) an ENTERPRISE intends TO dispose of BY sale, and TO components OF an enterprise THAT have BEEN disposed of OR classified AS held FOR sale.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s3"><span class="num">3</span><h2>Held-for-Sale Classification Criteria</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Genuine, imminent commitment to sell</div><div class="check-list"><span>Management, having appropriate authority, is committed to a plan to sell the asset</span><span>The asset is available for immediate sale in its present condition</span><span>An active program to locate a buyer has been initiated</span><span>The sale is probable, and expected to complete within one year</span><span>The asset is being actively marketed at a reasonable price relative to its current fair value</span><span>It is unlikely that significant changes will be made to the plan, or that the plan will be withdrawn</span></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s4"><span class="num">4</span><h2>Measurement Once Held for Sale</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">Lower of carrying amount and fair value less costs to sell</div><div class="text-supporting">ONCE classified AS held FOR sale, an ASSET (or ASSET group) is MEASURED at the LOWER of ITS carrying AMOUNT and FAIR value LESS costs TO sell — WITH any WRITE-down recognized IMMEDIATELY as AN impairment LOSS.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s5"><span class="num">5</span><h2>No Further Depreciation While Held for Sale</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Depreciation ceases at the classification date</div><div class="text-supporting">AN asset CLASSIFIED as HELD for SALE is <strong>NOT</strong> further DEPRECIATED (or AMORTIZED) WHILE it REMAINS in THAT classification — CONSISTENT with the ASSET being MEASURED at a LOWER-of-cost-and-FAIR-value basis RATHER than THROUGH ongoing SYSTEMATIC allocation.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s6"><span class="num">6</span><h2>Discontinued Operations — Definition</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">A separate major line of business or geographical area</div><div class="text-supporting">A DISCONTINUED operation is a COMPONENT of an ENTERPRISE that EITHER has BEEN disposed OF or IS classified AS held FOR sale, AND represents a SEPARATE major LINE of BUSINESS or GEOGRAPHICAL area OF operations — OR is PART of a SINGLE, coordinated PLAN to DISPOSE of SUCH a SEPARATE major LINE of BUSINESS or GEOGRAPHICAL area.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s7"><span class="num">7</span><h2>Presentation of Discontinued Operations</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Separated from continuing operations within the Income Statement</div><div class="text-supporting">THE results OF a DISCONTINUED operation are PRESENTED separately WITHIN the INCOME Statement, DISTINCT from CONTINUING operations (SEE the COMPANION Section 1520 poster) — HELPING readers ASSESS the ONGOING, UNDERLYING earning POWER of the BUSINESS distinct FROM operations THAT are BEING wound DOWN or SOLD.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s8"><span class="num">8</span><h2>Worked Example — Classifying an Asset as Held for Sale</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Writing an asset down to fair value less costs to sell</div>
<div class="worked" style="margin-bottom:0;"><div class="wk-title">Example: A manufacturing facility being actively marketed</div><div class="wk-body">A company commits to a plan to sell an idle manufacturing facility, carrying amount $2,800,000, meeting all held-for-sale criteria. The facility's fair value less costs to sell is $2,500,000.</div><div class="wk-answer">The COMPANY writes the FACILITY down to $2,500,000, RECOGNIZING a $2,800,000 − $2,500,000 = <strong>$300,000</strong> impairment LOSS, and CEASES further DEPRECIATION WHILE the ASSET remains CLASSIFIED as HELD for SALE.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s9"><span class="num">9</span><h2>Worked Example — Presenting a Discontinued Operation</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Isolating the wound-down segment's results</div>
<div class="worked" style="margin-bottom:0;"><div class="wk-title">Example: Exiting a separate geographical division</div><div class="wk-body">A company sells its entire European division — a separate, distinct geographical area of operations — meeting the discontinued operations criteria. The division generated a $180,000 loss (including disposal costs) during the year, while continuing operations earned $2,100,000.</div><div class="wk-answer">The COMPANY presents INCOME from CONTINUING operations of $2,100,000, SEPARATELY presents the $180,000 LOSS from DISCONTINUED operations, ARRIVING at NET income of $2,100,000 − $180,000 = <strong>$1,920,000</strong> — CLEARLY distinguishing the ONGOING business FROM the EXITED division.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s10"><span class="num">10</span><h2>Disclosure Requirements</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">What Section 3475 requires</div><div class="check-list"><span>Description of assets or asset groups classified as held for sale, and the facts and circumstances of the sale</span><span>Results of discontinued operations, presented separately, including revenue, expenses, and any gain or loss on disposal</span><span>Impairment losses (and reversals, where the asset's fair value less costs to sell subsequently increases) recognized on held-for-sale assets</span></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s11"><span class="num">11</span><h2>Critical Judgments &amp; Estimates</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cn span2"><div class="ctitle cn">Where judgment matters most</div>
<div class="two-col"><div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT JUDGMENTS</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Whether all held-for-sale classification criteria are genuinely met</span><span>Whether a disposed or held-for-sale component genuinely represents a separate major line of business or geographical area</span></div></div>
<div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT ESTIMATES</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Fair value less costs to sell for a held-for-sale asset</span></div></div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s12"><span class="num">12</span><h2>Relationship to IFRS 5</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Comparison — ASPE Section 3475 vs IFRS 5</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Feature</span><span style="color:var(--color-text-warning);">ASPE Section 3475</span><span style="color:var(--color-text-info);">IFRS 5</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Held-for-sale classification criteria</span><span>Broadly similar cumulative criteria</span><span>Broadly similar cumulative criteria — converged</span></div>
<div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Measurement basis</span><span>Lower of carrying amount and fair value less costs to sell</span><span>Lower of carrying amount and fair value less costs to sell — converged</span></div>
</div>
<div class="note">A GENUINELY thoroughly CONVERGED standard — the CORE classification and MEASUREMENT mechanics CLOSELY mirror the INTERNATIONAL approach, WITH no MEANINGFUL substantive DIVERGENCE to REPORT.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s13"><span class="num">13</span><h2>Statement Mapping</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">Where every disposal/discontinued operations event lands</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Event</span><span>Statement(s) affected</span><span>Notes</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Held-for-sale write-down</span><span><span class="badge bs">BS</span> <span class="badge is">IS</span></span><span>Impairment loss recognized immediately</span></div>
<div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Discontinued operations results</span><span><span class="badge is">IS</span></span><span>Presented separately from continuing operations</span></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s14"><span class="num">14</span><h2>Related Standards</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Cross-reference map</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>Section</span><span>Connection</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>Section 1520</span><span>Income Statement — governs the overall presentation this Section's discontinued operations separation feeds into</span></div>
<div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>Section 3063</span><span>Impairment of Long-lived Assets — a related, but distinct, impairment framework for assets remaining in use</span></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s15"><span class="num">15</span><h2>Quick-Reference Glossary</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cn span2">
<div class="glossary-item"><div class="glossary-term">Held for sale</div><div class="glossary-def">A classification for a long-lived asset whose carrying amount will be recovered principally through sale, rather than continuing use, meeting specific cumulative criteria.</div></div>
<div class="glossary-item" style="border-bottom:none;"><div class="glossary-term">Discontinued operation</div><div class="glossary-def">A component of an enterprise, representing a separate major line of business or geographical area, that has been disposed of or is classified as held for sale.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="legend"><div class="ltitle">Financial statement key (ASPE terminology)</div><div class="lrow"><div class="litem"><span class="badge bs">BS</span> Balance Sheet </div><div class="litem"><span class="badge is">IS</span> Income Statement </div><div class="litem"><span class="badge sre">SRE</span> Statement of Retained Earnings / Statement of Changes in Equity </div><div class="litem"><span class="badge scf">SCF</span> Cash Flow Statement</div></div></div>


</div>
  <section id="history">
    <HistoryTimeline items={history.aspe3475 || []} />
  </section>
</StandardPageLayout>
